# Reduce merge churn on CI-generated and CI-enriched data files.
# The enrichment pipeline (scripts/enrich_geojson.js) and the converter
# (convertAmt2gmaps.sh) both rewrite these files in full on every run,
# so on a merge conflict the right answer is "regenerate on the next
# CI run" — never a hand-merged JSON.
#
# We deliberately avoid `merge=union` here: union concatenates the
# conflicting hunks line-by-line, which on JSON produces syntactically
# invalid output (duplicated braces, dangling commas) that would
# silently break the loader. Marking the files as binary-style merge
# (-merge) makes git refuse to auto-merge and surface a conflict
# instead, which the CI regenerator then resolves cleanly.
*.geojson                -merge
ways_*.json              -merge
*.enrichment.meta.json   -merge
